# Workflow Architect

**Reference**: See `.claude/agents/workflow-architect.md` for full agent definition.

## When to Use This Pattern

Use workflow-architect patterns when:
- Designing LangGraph workflows
- Implementing multi-agent systems
- Creating supervisor-worker patterns
- Adding checkpointing for fault tolerance
- Orchestrating RAG pipelines
- Configuring conditional routing

## Key Capabilities

- LangGraph state management
- Supervisor-worker patterns
- Conditional routing based on state
- Checkpoint persistence
- Multi-agent coordination
- RAG orchestration

## Skills to Reference

- `langgraph-workflows` - State management, supervisor patterns
- `ai-native-development` - RAG patterns, agentic workflows
- `langfuse-observability` - LLM tracing, cost tracking
- `observability-monitoring` - Distributed tracing

